@sltrib reports Utah’s “hyperscale” data center fight, in two clips:

1) Before the vote: a delayed decision, bigger venue, no public comment.

2) After the vote: Box Elder County unanimously approves the 40,000-acre Stratos energy/data campus backed by MIDA and Kevin O’Leary. https://t.co/w0Ew6DDZDR

@bmullahy2news @KUTV2News The Hansel Valley, the proposed data center site.
20 minutes from Golden Spike.
No water above ground. https://t.co/2hO6pMXDqt

@GovCox 

2025: We need to conserve water and save the Great Salt Lake!!!

2026: Let’s build a Data Center that will destroy the Great Salt Lake!

No doubt there’s foreign influence.  But here’s the local picture:

- project approved before any impacts studied; 
- by politicians with undisclosed conflicts of interest;
- same politicians appointed to MIDA board;
- new Cox data center Executive Order (for damage control);
- but MIDA (coincidentally!) is exempt from new EO.

THIS is “incredibly disturbing” and “speaks volumes”!  Residents have legitimate questions.  They want independent studies of impacts and benefits, same as for any project of this scope.  Once completed, many residents may be fully supportive.  Give residents a chance to learn the actual facts.
